# {{place|en|One of the six <<states>> of <<c/Australia>>|capital=Sydney}}. Situated in the south-eastern part of the continent.
# {{lb|en|historical}} (1770—1850s) The original name conferred on Australia by [[w:Captain James Cook|Captain James Cook]], and used to describe the entire eastern portion of the continent.
# {{lb|en|historical}} (1788—1901) The [[colony]] that was founded in 1788, which grew progressively smaller as other colonies were separated from it, and became a [[state]] in 1901.
# {{lb|en|historical}} (1631–?) The name of an area of modern [[Canada]] stretching from the {{w|Nelson River}} in [[Manitoba]] to the {{w|James Bay}} in [[Ontario]].

